{{also|blood-thirsty}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|blood-thirsty}}
* {{qualifier|obsolete}} [[bloudthirsty]], [[bloud-thirsty]]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|blood|thirsty|lang=en}}. Compare {{cog|nl|bloeddorstig||bloodthirsty}}, {{cog|de|blutdürstig||bloodthirsty}}, {{cog|da|blodtørstig||bloodthirsty}}, {{cog|sv|blodtörstig||bloodthristy}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[thirsty|Thirsty]] for [[blood]]: [[inexorably]] [[violent]] or [[eager]] for [[bloodshed]], [[murderous]].
#* {{quote-web|date=2017-10-27|author=Alex McLevy|title=Making a killing: The brief life and bloody death of the post-Scream slasher revival|site=The Onion AV Club|url=https://www.avclub.com/making-a-killing-the-brief-life-and-bloody-death-of-th-1819784777|passage= The slasher narrative is as simple as a knife in the head: Some tragic event creates a killer who then seeks '''bloodthirsty''' revenge for that primal trauma, and audiences hoot and cringe in equal measure as characters lose their lives one by one, often in unexpected or inventive ways, until a resourceful “Final Girl” manages to defeat the monster. }}

